    "what_went_wrong": "The comparator resolver hardcoded the float32 k-shot FILENAME. That arm OOM-killed and banked under a bf16 name, so the resolver silently skipped it, chose the schema arm at 0.8958, and printed reading (a). The frozen rule is 'the better of the two prompted 3B arms' -- named as a rule precisely so no number could be typed in -- and the k-shot arm was on disk at 0.9747, in the SAME dtype as the adapted arm, which is the exact within-dtype comparison the frozen contingency demands. The printed (a) stood for roughly thirty minutes.",
