    "frozen_reading_applied": "(b) IT WAS A SMALL-MODEL CRUTCH. By the row's own letter: the sign test fails to separate the arms at p <= 0.05 (p=0.1445), which is (b)'s second disjunct. Both statistics publish: the mean is -0.0390 -- direction against adaptation, magnitude past the tolerance -- while 22 of 30 documents tie. (c) does not fire because the sign test does not agree; (d) does not fire because the statistics point the same way, one merely without significance. Addendum O's verdict extends to this rung: at 3B, adaptation buys nothing that good prompting does not already have.",
    "what_the_adapted_arm_still_shows": "0.9356 with 0 invalid is the highest adapted score this project has produced, and it beats the schema-prompted 3B by +0.0398 with a passing sign test (13W/4L/13T, p=0.0245) -- adaptation DOES beat schema-only prompting at 3B. What it does not beat is 20 demonstrations. The live engineering question moves to the preregistered ladder: does adaptation PLUS demonstrations beat demonstrations alone (rung E3), and does more training move it (rung E2)."
